From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 16:42:23 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 76/76] flashnext cuda: --tp 2's out projections cut by input
 columns, the two partials added once, behind TF_FLASHNEXT_OUTPROJ_KSPLIT

Not bit-exact: each rank projects its own heads over its input columns of out_proj and o_proj, and one exchange
(the peer's mapped buffer, or NCCL's two-rank sum) adds the FP32 partials, so both ranks hold the same rows but the
sums differ from the whole dot products. Default off.
